<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>FTRL</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm is initialized with the following parameters: number of arms <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{arms}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>arms</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{arms}}</annotation></semantics></math>, dimension <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, exploration parameter <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and regularization parameters <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The cumulative gradient vectors for each arm are stored in <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, initialized as zero vectors of dimension <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The weight vector <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> for each arm <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is computed as:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=\begin{cases}-\frac{z_{i}-\text{sign}(z_{i})\cdot l_{1}}{\frac{\beta+\sqrt{n_{i}}}{\alpha}+l_{2}}&amp;\text{if }|z_{i}|&gt;l_{1}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>sign</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=\begin{cases}-\frac{z_{i}-\text{sign}(z_{i})\cdot l_{1}}{\frac{\beta+\sqrt{n_{i}}}{\alpha}+l_{2}}&amp;\text{if }|z_{i}|&gt;l_{1}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cumulative gradient for the <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th feature of arm <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cumulative squared gradient for the <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th feature. The arm with the highest score, calculated as the dot product of the weight vector <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> and the context vector, is selected:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}=\arg\max_{a\in\{1,\ldots,n_{\text{arms}}\}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}w_{i}\cdot\mathbf{x}_{i}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>arms</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}=\arg\max_{a\in\{1,\ldots,n_{\text{arms}}\}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}w_{i}\cdot\mathbf{x}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving a reward <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for the selected arm <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the algorithm updates the cumulative gradient vector <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math> and the squared gradient sum <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐧</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for the selected arm:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{error}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{error}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle w,\mathbf{x}\rangle-r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle w,\mathbf{x}\rangle-r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{error}\cdot\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{error}\cdot\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{n_{i}+g_{i}^{2}}-\sqrt{n_{i}}}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{n_{i}+g_{i}^{2}}-\sqrt{n_{i}}}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leftarrow z_{i}+g_{i}-\sigma\cdot w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leftarrow z_{i}+g_{i}-\sigma\cdot w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leftarrow n_{i}+g_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leftarrow n_{i}+g_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This formulation allows the FTRL algorithm to adaptively adjust the exploration-exploitation trade-off by incorporating both the cumulative reward and the uncertainty in the form of regularization terms, which are scaled by the learning rate <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and exploration parameter <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span><math id="A4.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-Greedy Follow-The-Regularized-Leader (FTRL) Bandit Policy</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each round <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe a contextual feature vector <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and must choose an arm <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each arm <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, the algorithm maintains a weight vector <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> summarizing past feedback for that arm. We write</p>
<table id="A4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k,t-1}=\{(x_{s},r_{s}):s&lt;t,a_{s}=k\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k,t-1}=\{(x_{s},r_{s}):s&lt;t,a_{s}=k\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for the history of rounds in which arm <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> was selected, where <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the observed reward.
Given <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the current weights <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{k,t}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{k,t}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, FTRL defines a score for each arm via a linear model</p>
<table id="A4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{k,t}=x_{t}^{\top}w_{k,t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{k,t}=x_{t}^{\top}w_{k,t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We then apply an <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy rule with exploration parameter <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{t}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{t}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.i1.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:2.2pt;"><math id="A4.I2.i1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\blacktriangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>▶</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\blacktriangleright</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With probability <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\varepsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\varepsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose the greedy arm</p>
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}=\arg\max_{k\in\{1,\dots,K\}}\hat{r}_{k,t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}=\arg\max_{k\in\{1,\dots,K\}}\hat{r}_{k,t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.i2.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:2.2pt;"><math id="A4.I2.i2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\blacktriangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>▶</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\blacktriangleright</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With probability <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose a uniformly random arm from <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">In our experiments we use a fixed <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A4.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0.10</annotation></semantics></math>), but standard decaying schedules such as <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{t}=\min\{1,c/\sqrt{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{t}=\min\{1,c/\sqrt{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are also compatible with the framework.
After selecting <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and observing reward <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we update only the parameters associated with the chosen arm. Let</p>
<table id="A4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}=-\,r_{t}\,x_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}=-\,r_{t}\,x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">denote the (linear) loss gradient for arm <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. FTRL defines the next iterate <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{a_{t},t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{a_{t},t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> as the solution of a regularized cumulative optimization problem:</p>
<table id="A4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{a_{t},t+1}~=~\arg\min_{w\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left\{\sum_{s\leq t:a_{s}=a_{t}}g_{s}^{\top}w~+~\lambda\,\Omega(w)\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.608em" rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mi>arg</mi><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.552em" rspace="0.552em">+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{a_{t},t+1}~=~\arg\min_{w\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left\{\sum_{s\leq t:a_{s}=a_{t}}g_{s}^{\top}w~+~\lambda\,\Omega(w)\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex regularizer and <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a regularization coefficient. In our implementation we use an <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-regularizer, <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(w)=\tfrac{1}{2}\|w\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(w)=\tfrac{1}{2}\|w\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields a closed-form solution equivalent to online ridge regression over past rewards for that arm:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{a_{t},t+1}=\left(\lambda I+\sum_{s\leq t:a_{s}=a_{t}}x_{s}x_{s}^{\top}\right)^{-1}\left(\sum_{s\leq t:a_{s}=a_{t}}r_{s}x_{s}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{a_{t},t+1}=\left(\lambda I+\sum_{s\leq t:a_{s}=a_{t}}x_{s}x_{s}^{\top}\right)^{-1}\left(\sum_{s\leq t:a_{s}=a_{t}}r_{s}x_{s}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Weights for all other arms <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\neq a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\neq a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> remain unchanged, i.e., <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k,t+1}=w_{k,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k,t+1}=w_{k,t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy FTRL variant thus behaves like a linear contextual bandit with a ridge-regularized FTRL learner for each arm, combined with a simple <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy exploration mechanism. In practice, we do not recompute the closed-form solution from scratch; instead, we maintain sufficient statistics for each arm and update them incrementally.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Linear EXP3</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm is initialized with parameters: number of arms <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{arms}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>arms</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{arms}}</annotation></semantics></math>, dimension <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, exploration parameter <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, and learning rate <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Each arm <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> maintains a parameter vector <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, initialized as <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We compute the probability distribution over arms using the following formulation:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{logits}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>logits</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{logits}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\theta_{a}^{\top}\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\theta_{a}^{\top}\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A4.Ex30.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">logits</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{logits}-\max(\text{logits})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>logits</mtext><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>logits</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{logits}-\max(\text{logits})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{exp\_logits}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>exp_logits</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{exp\_logits}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp(\text{logits}_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>logits</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp(\text{logits}_{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{base\_probs}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>base_probs</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{base\_probs}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{exp\_logits}_{a}}{\sum_{a=1}^{n_{\text{arms}}}\text{exp\_logits}_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mtext>exp_logits</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>arms</mtext></msub></msubsup><msub><mtext>exp_logits</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{exp\_logits}_{a}}{\sum_{a=1}^{n_{\text{arms}}}\text{exp\_logits}_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{probs}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>probs</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{probs}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\gamma)\cdot\text{base\_probs}_{a}+\frac{\gamma}{n_{\text{arms}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>base_probs</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>arms</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\gamma)\cdot\text{base\_probs}_{a}+\frac{\gamma}{n_{\text{arms}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is the context vector. The arm is selected based on the probability distribution <span id="A4.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">probs</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A4.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">update</span> method updates the parameter vector <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> for the selected arm <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> using the estimated reward <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{r}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{r}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{r_{t}}{p_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{r_{t}}{p_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leftarrow\theta_{a}+\eta\cdot\hat{r}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leftarrow\theta_{a}+\eta\cdot\hat{r}_{t}\cdot\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability of selecting arm <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the received reward. This strategy leverages exponential weighting and exploration bonuses to balance exploration and exploitation in a linear contextual setting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Linear FTPL</h3>

<div id="A4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm is initialized with parameters: number of arms <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{arms}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>arms</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{arms}}</annotation></semantics></math>, dimension <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, and learning rate <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Each arm <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> maintains a parameter vector <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, initialized as <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A4.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">select_arm</span> method computes the perturbed scores for each arm using the following formulation:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{linear\_score}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>linear_score</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{linear\_score}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\theta_{a}^{\top}\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\theta_{a}^{\top}\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{noise}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>noise</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{noise}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\text{Gumbel}(0,\frac{1}{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Gumbel</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\text{Gumbel}(0,\frac{1}{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{score}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>score</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{score}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{linear\_score}_{a}+\text{noise}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>linear_score</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>noise</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{linear\_score}_{a}+\text{noise}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is the context vector. The arm with the highest perturbed score is selected:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}=\arg\max_{a\in\{1,\ldots,n_{\text{arms}}\}}\text{score}_{a}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>arms</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mtext>score</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}=\arg\max_{a\in\{1,\ldots,n_{\text{arms}}\}}\text{score}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{a}\leftarrow\theta_{a}+r_{t}\cdot\mathbf{x}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{a}\leftarrow\theta_{a}+r_{t}\cdot\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This strategy leverages random perturbations from a Gumbel distribution to balance exploration and exploitation, allowing the algorithm to explore suboptimal arms while exploiting the accumulated knowledge of their performance in a linear contextual setting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.7 </span>Thompson Sampling</h3>

<div id="A4.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a given <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, sample <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\theta}a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{a},\Sigma_{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\theta}a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{a},\Sigma_{a})</annotation></semantics></math> and select the arm maximizing:</p>
<table id="A4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{*}=\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbf{x}^{\top}\tilde{\theta}_{a}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{*}=\argmax_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\mathbf{x}^{\top}\tilde{\theta}_{a}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Standard Bayesian linear regression updates are then used to update <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the observed reward <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A4.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E8X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{a}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{a}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E8X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leftarrow\Sigma_{a}^{-1}+\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}\,\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leftarrow\Sigma_{a}^{-1}+\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}\,\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E8Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E8Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E8Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leftarrow\Sigma_{a}\Bigl(\Sigma_{a}^{-1}\mu_{a}+\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}\,\mathbf{x}\,r\Bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leftarrow\Sigma_{a}\Bigl(\Sigma_{a}^{-1}\mu_{a}+\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}\,\mathbf{x}\,r\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T7.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage</span></td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T7.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Median Tokens</span></td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T7.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mean Tokens</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Original query (input)</td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">16</td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">19.3</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Feature-tagger output</td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">110</td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">110.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Rewrite input</td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">26</td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">29.3</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Rewrite output</td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">18</td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">28.1</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Answer input</td>
<td id="A4.T7.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">64</td>
